@alculquicondor To my understanding, we will remove the data stored in PodBackOffMap, and the PodBackOffMap can be refactored as something like:

```
type PodBackoff struct {
	// initial backoff duration
	initialDuration time.Duration
	// maximal backoff duration
	maxDuration time.Duration
}
```

Is this what you expected?

But after that podBackoff.GetBackoffTime can not check if a pod is inside the podBackoff structure, so the value of "exists" won't be false, this will cause some tests in scheduler_queue_test.go to be failed. There are many places in the test in which `movePodsToActiveOrBackoffQueue` was assumed to move all pods to active queue because pod info doesn't exist in the old podBackoffMap structure, after this change, `movePodsToActiveOrBackoffQueue` actually move all pods to backoff queue.

```
func (p *PriorityQueue) isPodBackingOff(pod *v1.Pod) bool {
	boTime, exists := p.podBackoff.GetBackoffTime(nsNameForPod(pod))
 	if !exists {
 		return false // this won't return false now and cause pod to be moved to backoff queue
 	}
 	return boTime.After(p.clock.Now())
 }
```

